{"availability":"available","full":"weave-registry/wardian","name":"wardian","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-08T20:23:05Z","updated":"2026-10-09T22:01:34Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://wardian-gold.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://wardian-gold.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.706Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.706Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.706Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.706Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Wardian keeps the small tools you make, often with AI, on a computer you control. It serves them to your browser from a local folder or straight from Google Drive. Each app runs sealed: it cannot see your files or your other apps unless you allow it, and the browser blocks its requests to anywhere but its own package (three narrow routes stay open; /docs/security lists them). The full documentation is at /docs on a running Wardian.","The name comes from the Wardian case, the sealed glass case that let living plants travel safely across oceans in the 1800s. Your apps are the plants; Wardian is the case.","Wardian was called rustle before version 0.4. The rustle command still works and runs wardian, /sdk/rustle.js still loads, and .rustle files still import."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/weave-registry/wardian/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a468d493eadbbbe4ff9ff0703c7d1bc39ca07d1c5a42fa6782a6353dc0e920eb","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.814Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.814Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Wardian keeps the small tools you make, often with AI, on a computer you control. It serves them to your browser from a local folder or straight from Google Drive. Each app runs sealed: it cannot see your files or your other apps unless you allow it, and the browser blocks its requests to anywhere but its own package (three narrow routes stay open; /docs/security lists them). The full documentation is at /docs on a running Wardian.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/weave-registry/wardian/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Then run wardian start --at-login: Wardian runs in the background, starts again each time you log in, and opens in your browser (wardian stop ends it; plain wardian runs it in the terminal instead).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/weave-registry/wardian/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The details (who counts as an admin, the data folder, where apps come from, the start and stop records) go to wardian.log in the data folder. --no-open or WARDIANNOOPEN=1 keeps the browser closed; NOCOLOR=1 or TERM=dumb turns colour off.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/weave-registry/wardian/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"a468d493eadbbbe4ff9ff0703c7d1bc39ca07d1c5a42fa6782a6353dc0e920eb","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/weave-registry/wardian/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.814Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T22:01:34Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/weave-registry/wardian/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.817Z","hash":"a468d493eadbbbe4ff9ff0703c7d1bc39ca07d1c5a42fa6782a6353dc0e920eb","originalBytes":39556,"storedBytes":39556,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["wardian","app","apps","folder","splunk","data","key","each","one","file","settings","start","page","every","runs","browser","claude","only","tests","token","open","run","when","bedrock","them","set","api","admin","own","search","none","drive","needs","server","shows","version","back","import","keeps","keys","opens","press","saved","stop","address","first","other","release","same","see","table","what","any","it.","never","rows","service","where